Abstract—This proposed work explores the application of augmented reality (AR) for indoor navigation in emergency situations and large spaces using Unity NavMesh and the A* algorithm. It provides real-time information about college classrooms and enhances accessibility for people with disabilities. The proposed system utilizes Vuforia and Unity to construct the AR environment, integrating QR code scanning using the ZXING SDK, as well as the smart control of light bulbs, fans, and other appliances through ESP32, relay modules, and the Blynk API. Experimental results demonstrate the effectiveness of our approach in improving navigation accuracy and accessibility for users. Furthermore, the system’s real-time updates, user-friendly interface, and remote appliance control offer a versatile solution for various indoor environments. The proposed work presents a detailed explanation of the literature review, the operating architecture, discusses its social impact, limitations, and future scope, highlighting its potential to revolutionize indoor navigation and accessibility for all.
Keywords- Augmented Reality, Indoor Navigation, Unity NavMesh, A* Algorithm, Accessibility, QR Code Scanning, ESP32, Blynk API, Experimental Results.
I. INTRODUCTION
In various settings, including educational institutions, hospitals, shopping centers, and business buildings, indoor navigation presents significant challenges. Finding the quickest route to safety in an emergency is essential, yet effectively maneuvering in large areas can be challenging. Traditional navigation systems often fall short in providing real-time information updates and meeting the needs of people with impairments. This paper proposes an indoor navigation system based on augmented reality that includes real-time data, remote appliance control, and enhanced accessibility features to address these limitations.
Navigating complex indoor spaces has long been a challenge. Traditional methods rely on static signs and limited visual cues, leaving users to navigate through unfamiliar environments. This work aims to revolutionize indoor navigation by leveraging augmented reality. By overlaying real-

time guidance and information directly onto users’ field of vision, our system empowers individuals to confidently and efficiently navigate indoor spaces, even in high-stress emergency situations. Through the utilization of Unity NavMesh and the A* algorithm, users can access dynamic route suggestions, ensuring they reach their destinations.
In conjunction with indoor navigation, our proposed system seamlessly integrates with the Internet of Things (IoT). By connecting to smart appliances within indoor spaces, users gain unparalleled control over their surroundings. Through ESP32, relay modules, and the Blynk API, our system allows users to remotely manage lighting, climate control, and other devices, optimizing energy usage, enhancing comfort, and ensuring a personalized indoor environment.
Key Contributions: • Enhanced Indoor Navigation: The paper introduces an
augmented reality-based indoor navigation system that utilizes Unity NavMesh and the A* algorithm. This system significantly improves navigation accuracy, providing real-time guidance and information to users in emergency situations and large spaces, addressing the challenges of traditional navigation methods. • Accessibility and IoT Integration: The proposed system goes beyond navigation by seamlessly integrating with the Internet of Things (IoT). Users can remotely control lighting, climate, and other appliances through ESP32, relay modules, and the Blynk API, enhancing accessibility for all individuals and offering personalized indoor environments. • Social Impact and Future Potential: The system’s contributions extend to public safety, inclusivity for people with disabilities, and energy efficiency. It has the potential to revolutionize indoor navigation and transform indoor spaces into responsive environments. Future enhancements could involve wearable devices, integration with emergency services, and further customization options for users.

